The decay $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$, which is extremely difficult to study experimentally, has a branching ratio that is highly dependent on the results of $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ decays within the leptoquark $U_1$ model. There are four distinct categories of form factors that significantly influence the branching ratio and other observables associated with $b 	o c$ transitions as well as $b 	o c$ transitions. Given the current constraints on $b 	o c$ transitions, very high values of the leptoquark mass, greater than 9 times the standard weak interaction scale, are required to achieve viable values for the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay's branching ratio and other related parameters.
